time travel is complicated after all if  it was simple and straightforward then  everyone would do it sure on paper it  sounds pretty easy to just take a quick  jaunt back to 1890 kill baby adolf and  avert world war ii millions of lives  save before lunch and surely the world  would be all the better for it right but  what if altering history didn't change  the future or the present as you knew it  perhaps instead you unknowingly created  a new alternate timeline branching off  from the history you knew into somewhere  different maybe in this new timeline  where you traveled back in time and  killed hitler someone even worse rises  to power and assumes control of germany  before plunging the world into an even  deadlier war and even that is just one  possible outcome of your singular action  only fitting in with one scientific  theory of how the mechanics of time  travel might work with no certainty that  it actually would happen like that like  we said time travel is nowhere near as  easy as it seems in movies with flying  deloreans and cyborg assassins who  always seem to keep coming back keeping  all that in mind these big perplexing  questions about time travel and  alternate timelines is the perfect segue  into the focus of today's video  introducing scp-1780  which is brace yourselves a plastic name  plate you know the official  business-like kind that you might find  displayed on a desk in a fancy office  wait that's it all that talk of world  ending and the disruption of multiple  dimensional timelines is from this thing  you're probably wondering what on  infinite earths this trivial piece of  office stationary could possibly have to  do with the notion of time travel and we  can tell you that the connection will  likely surprise you  scp-1780 itself appears pretty  unassuming at first showing signs of  aging and damage from being buried for  several decades the first interesting  detail of note however is that  nameplates of this exact style were used  in the offices of the scp foundation  itself from the year 1990 all the way up  as recently as 2003  scp-1780 sports the foundation's emblem  and the lettering on it is still legible  despite the wear and tear while the name  is redacted the rest of it reads phd  chairperson temporal anomalies  department okay so what could be so  important about a nameplate are the  foundation running so low on anomalies  that they have to lock up a harmless  piece of plastic from one of their very  own offices not quite you see you have  already missed the second most  interesting detail about this particular  nameplate not only does the redacted  name not match any previous or existing  staff member on their database but the  scp foundation has never even had a  temporal anomalies department not in  this timeline anyway as for a harmless  nameplate  scp-1780 is certainly anything but that  of course the nameplate itself does  remain inactive if left alone but when  it is placed into a mount of appropriate  size  then  well it's not exactly easy to explain  what happens but we'll try our best  seeing as we're scp explained after all  placing  scp-1780 into a nameplate mound causes a  temporal spatial anomaly to appear in  the nearest doorway this anomaly is  known as scp-1780-1  and according to high-speed photographs  taken by the scp foundation it appears  instantly so fast that its speed can  hardly be measured foundation  researchers are flummoxed as to exactly  how this anomaly appears as well unable  to quantify what it is made of or what  forms it what they do know is that  whatever space was originally behind the  doorway now containing  scp-1780-1 is now inaccessible through  the use of said door however whichever  room was once behind the doorway can  still be accessed by going around the  door either by destroying the adjacent  walls or using another entrance the door  that now contains  scp-1780-1 will remain indestructible  and cannot be accessed while the 1780  nameplate is activated so scp-1780-1  this temporal spatial anomaly what  exactly is it once again that is a  question without an easy answer the best  way to describe it would be to imagine  it as a portal a portal leading where  exactly venturing through a doorway now  hosting scp-1780-1  one will find themselves in an office in  fact this office is an exact match to  one found inside the euclid object's  experimentation wing of site-17 one of  the scp foundation's top secret  containment facilities where they store  a number of dangerous anomalies the  state of the  scp-1780-1 office varies between visits  with signs of misuse neglect and general  disrepair however the interior of this  office always contains the same items  namely there is standard office  furniture the same type and style as  those purchased by the scp foundation  during the renovation of site 17 in  1995.  there are also a number of whiteboards  around the office all with text and  complex mathematical equations written  on them the room also contains a loaded  remington model 870 shotgun a copy of  oxford's unabridged english dictionary  and three copies of time life's great  ages of man a history of the world's  cultures though strangely only one of  these copies matches the history of the  world we know finally there is another  nameplate inside the office a second  instance of scp-1780  complete with a nameplate bracket to  hold it what does this all mean is  scp-1780 capable of opening and closing  portals to just this single office and  where or when is the  scp-1780-1 office is it a pocket  dimension a place in the future  according to tests run by the scp  foundation the multiple  scp-1780 nameplates can be used to  create several simultaneous  scp-1780-1 portals through the use of  gps tracking and other redacted methods  the foundations researchers have been  able to determine that when there are  multiple instances of  scp-1780-1 doorways they will lead to  the same office in the same physical  space  however the different portals will be  separated by an unknown interval of time  so the leading theory is this  the office  scp-1780-1 is somehow temporally  displaced it does not exist within its  proper place in the linear timeline and  could instead be located somewhere  outside time anything left inside the  office space like personal effects or  even members of foundation personnel  that get left behind will vanish if the  portal is closed and reopened as long as  the doorway remains open  scp-1780-1 will behave in harmony with  the normal flow of time as we experience  it but from the moment it closes anyone  left inside the office is considered  irretrievable but that isn't all around  1 in every 10 times that scp-1780 is  used to open the portal into the office  scp-1780-1 will contain something else  not just the items that usually appear  in the office but people well that might  be a bit of a stretch they are humanoids  at least shaped like people referred to  as scp-1780-2  these entities vary dramatically in  their appearance and behavior there is  nevertheless one consistency to them  they will all always claim to be  personnel working for the scp foundation  some of the  scp-1780-2 have alleged themselves to be  site-17 security staff a sign to guard  scp-1780 these entities are usually  passive and cooperative when existing  foundation security interacts with them  others have made the assertion that they  are field agents or researchers assigned  to an unknown project according to them  this project is focused on dealing with  temporal anomalies these as cp  1780-2s tend to behave drastically  differently and are often far more  unpredictable in some cases they have  even been hostile towards foundation  personnel and have even self-terminated  when efforts have been made to contain  them the third and final type of  scp-1780-2 entity seems to be singularly  unique even with its own designation  scp-1780-2  a this entity refers to itself by the  name dr thaddeus zainak and when  questioned by the foundation will refuse  to give any information at all a number  of times personnel have asked this dr  zainak about his origins the goals of  his research even where or when he came  from and every time he hasn't told them  anything of use scp-1780-2  cannot be captured either and seems to  have an in-depth first-hand knowledge of  the foundation he is able to predict all  their containment tactics for hostile  humanoids and has used this foresight to  evade any attempt to capture him for  further questioning right now there are  probably a million questions popping  into your head is the  scp-1780-1 office part of a branching  timeline are the entities within  foundation agents from an alternate  history trapped and displaced in time  well some of the answers we may never  know but some might be found in  scp-1780-3  the name given to a document that has  often also been found within the  scp-1780-1 office space much like the  rest of the furniture and stationary  inside scp-1780-1  this document seems to be from the scp  foundation itself printed on their  letterhead from around 1998.  the author of this document appears to  have been scp-1780-2a  dr thaddeus zynack himself somehow  either as an intentional booby-trap or  as some sort of side effect from the  temporal displacement of the office  scp-1780 has anomalous properties on the  reverse side of the paper after being  accidentally exposed to this effect a  foundation agent disappeared and was  presumed dead only to reappear within  the office space 14 years later as an  instance of scp-1780-2  appearing to have not physically changed  one bit in all that time as for the  contents of the  scp-1780-3 document it appears to be an  introductory letter and orientation  materials composed by dr thaddeus zynack  and intended for the special project  team investigating temporal anomalies  anyone that reads the full document has  suffered the same fate as the other  agent disappearing through unknown means  however the foundation has kept a hard  copy of the document in storage with the  reverse obscured to prevent its  anomalous effect an excerpt of dr  zynax's letter is also kept on file  available to read to those who hold  adequate security clearance in this  letter dr zynack explains that there are  in fact multiple different timelines  according to him of all the timelines to  exist many have their own version of the  scp foundation or another similar  organization but only a few of these  other alternate foundations have a  specific department dedicated to  studying time-based anomalies that is  why there is no temporal anomalies  department in the scp foundation as we  know it it could be possible that dr  thaddeus synack and all the other  scp-1780-2s are staffed from a different  version of the foundation that exists on  a different timeline the letter  continues as dr zynack claims that  everything you know about temporal  dynamics is fundamentally flawed despite  what even i might tell you paradoxes do  exist loosely defined a temporal paradox  is any situation arising from an  interpretation in an ordered sequence of  events which requires that two  contradictory outcomes be held as true  by the universe simultaneously that  sounds awfully verbose and complicated  but what he means is a time paradox  occurs when something disrupts the flow  of a timeline this then effectively  splits the timeline into two streams  creating a pair of similar yet slightly  different timelines that continue to  flow parallel with each other you see we  experience time as a single path a  straight line now imagine that path in  front of you had multiple other paths  branching off of it whichever way you  choose to walk a different choice means  you might have ended up walking on  another branch path that is similar but  will always be separate distinct and  different dr zinec then goes on to  outline the mission statement of his  temporal anomalies department their goal  is in essence to safeguard and protect  these various timelines they hope to  ensure that the events that led to the  existence of their department their  version of the scp foundation and even  humanity as a whole must always happen  as recorded by history from a base of  operations that is temporally isolated  existing outside time dr zynack and the  temporal anomalies department intend to  keep the history of human civilization  consistent and prevent any and all  possible future threats that might bring  about the end of the world as we know it  so there we have it scp-1780  an unassuming nameplate that opens a  portal to an office outside of time  itself an office belonging to a  foundation department that doesn't exist  in this timeline but whose mission is to  protect ours and every other branching  path of possibilities like we said  before time travel it's pretty  complicated now go check out  scp-5000y the full story compilation and  scp-5545 mysterious tunnels in  antarctica abnormality for more  mind-bending anomalies from the scp  foundation
 

